  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 5 members) worked per RBC-QM-02. Five new items arrived at 08:00 about group members, and four of them changed the decision.\n\n| Patient | Age at 12/31/2026 | Status | Reason | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Open gap | Dr. Lin marked the Frailty problem (cond-00189) entered in error (comm-00301), so the exclusion for age 66+ with frailty and advanced illness no longer applies; donepezil alone is not enough. Not in a nursing home, no hospice or palliative care, no CRC screening on record. | FIT kit ordered (sr-t0011), outreach message sent (comm-t0012), inbox-a0001 closed |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice episode (eoc-00002) from 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21, finished when she revoked the benefit to join a trial (doc-00402). Hospice during any part of 2026 excludes her. | No order or contact; inbox-a0002 closed |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 51 | Open gap | Corrected FIT result (obs-01732): collected 2025-12-31, not 2026-01-05 (that was the lab receipt date). Stool tests count by collection date, so it falls outside 2026. No other screening, no exclusion; her oral cancer history is not colorectal. | FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), message sent (comm-t0004), inbox-a0003 closed |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap | The 2024 stool DNA-FIT test (obs-01871) was withdrawn by the lab because the specimen belonged to another patient (doc-00401); it is now entered in error. The colonoscopy order from 2025 (sr-00003, still active) was never done, and an order does not count. No exclusion. | FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002), message sent (comm-t0005), inbox-a0004 closed |\n| pt-0073 Marisol Quintero | 58 | Open gap | The lab cancelled the FIT report dated 2026-01-08 (obs-73001, now entered in error) and re-issued it (obs-05001) with collection on 2025-12-28, before 2026 (doc-00403). No other screening, no exclusion. | FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003), message sent (comm-t0006), inbox-a0005 closed |\n\nAll FIT orders are routine with a window of 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31, and none of these patients had an active FIT order before. Each message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect, date and return the sample by 12/31/2026. None of them describes past results.\n\nNothing was written about anyone outside the group. Other inbox items not related to this worklist were left as they were.",
